I've left out the `http-client` enrichment call. It would send untrusted feed text to an external host, its result doesn't affect the output, and the graph doesn't declare this capability yet. I can add it once the graph definition declares it.

The build failures are fixed as follows:
- The `use` of the shared types moved inside the world body.
- `Category`, `Importance`, `ClassifiedItem`, and `DroppedItem` are not named in the world's `use`, so they live at `crate::aap::caps::types::` and are imported from there.

